window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-f37d22b64179d756"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"prioritize-drug-targets\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">优先排序药物靶点</h1> <p>综合多条证据线对药物靶点进行排序。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT 和 Life Science Research 插件规范化实体，并行检索遗传学、队列、临床、文献和表达证据；对各条证据线打分，最终给出可复用图表支持的排序结果。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要不止一类证据的靶点优先级问题，例如遗传学、队列重复验证、疾病背景、临床先例、文献和表达情况。</li> <li>希望 ChatGPT 跨多条证据线开展科学研究，再将结果整合为一个结论的团队。</li> <li>希望保存原始载荷、使用明确的评分标准，并生成可在下一次审阅或决策备忘录中复用图表的科学家。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Life Science Research（已阻止不安全链接）</td> <td>搜索科学数据库和文献，为通路、转化研究、可成药性及竞争情况等证据提供依据。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>优先排序哮喘药物靶点</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 Life Science Research 插件，对 TSLP、IL33 和 IL1RL1 进行比较，为哮喘药物靶点确定优先级。\n\n使用子代理并行运行以下互相独立的证据线：\n- 人类遗传学与 GWAS：gwas-catalog-skill、opentargets-skill、gnomad-graphql-skill\n- 队列重复验证与 PheWAS：finngen-phewas-skill、ukb-topmed-phewas-skill、biobankjapan-phewas-skill、tpmi-phewas-skill\n- 靶点—疾病证据与疾病背景：opentargets-skill、efo-ontology-skill\n- 临床和监管先例：clinicaltrials-skill、opentargets-skill、chembl-skill、pharmgkb-skill\n- 文献和公共数据集背景：ncbi-entrez-skill、ncbi-pmc-skill、biorxiv-skill、ncbi-datasets-skill、biostudies-arrayexpress-skill\n- 表达及组织/细胞类型背景：human-protein-atlas-skill、gtex-eqtl-skill、cellxgene-skill、bgee-skill\n\n对每条证据线：\n- 按 1–5 分别为 TSLP、IL33 和 IL1RL1 评分\n- 将直接的哮喘证据与相邻的过敏/特应性表型分开\n- 在有帮助时保存原始载荷\n\n然后综合整理：\n- 按证据线和靶点排列的评分表\n- TSLP、IL33、IL1RL1 的最终排名\n- 置信度评估和主要注意事项\n- 两张图：靶点优先级热图，以及显示每个靶点主要哮喘相关变异的 GWAS 摘要图\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/form/life-sciences-access/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">申请 GPT-Rosalind 访问权限（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"leverage-skills\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">使用技能</h2> <p><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/life-science-research\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Life Science Research 插件（需联网）</a>包含适用于各条证据线的技能：</p> <ul> <li>人类遗传学与 GWAS：<code>gwas-catalog-skill</code>、<code>opentargets-skill</code>、<code>gnomad-graphql-skill</code></li> <li>队列重复验证与 PheWAS：<code>finngen-phewas-skill</code>、<code>ukb-topmed-phewas-skill</code>、<code>biobankjapan-phewas-skill</code>、<code>tpmi-phewas-skill</code></li> <li>靶点—疾病证据与疾病背景：<code>opentargets-skill</code>、<code>efo-ontology-skill</code></li> <li>临床和监管先例：<code>clinicaltrials-skill</code>、<code>opentargets-skill</code>、<code>chembl-skill</code>、<code>pharmgkb-skill</code></li> <li>文献和公共数据集背景：<code>ncbi-entrez-skill</code>、<code>ncbi-pmc-skill</code>、<code>biorxiv-skill</code>、<code>ncbi-datasets-skill</code>、<code>biostudies-arrayexpress-skill</code></li> <li>表达及组织/细胞类型背景：<code>human-protein-atlas-skill</code>、<code>gtex-eqtl-skill</code>、<code>cellxgene-skill</code>、<code>bgee-skill</code></li> </ul> <p>你可以明确点名使用这些技能，也可以让 ChatGPT 自行决定何时使用。</p> <p><a id=\"step-by-step-guide\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">分步指南</h2> <ol> <li>提出具体的比较问题，并明确希望 ChatGPT 分析的靶点、疾病和证据线。</li> <li>调用 <code>Life Science Research</code> 插件，并让 ChatGPT 使用子代理并行运行这些证据线，使每一类证据的范围都清晰明确。</li> <li>让 ChatGPT 按固定的 1–5 分制给每条证据线打分，并将疾病直接证据与相邻表型分开。</li> <li>在同一聊天中审阅已保存的原始载荷、按证据线和靶点排列的评分表，以及汇总后的排名。</li> </ol>","en":"<h1 id=\"prioritize-drug-targets\">Prioritize drug targets</h1> <p>Rank drug targets across multiple evidence lanes.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with the Life Science Research plugin to normalize entities, retrieve genetics, cohort, clinical, literature, and expression evidence in parallel, score each lane, and produce a final ranking with reusable visuals.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Target prioritization questions that need more than one evidence family, such as genetics, cohort replication, disease context, clinical precedent, literature, and expression.</li> <li>Teams that want ChatGPT to perform scientific research across multiple evidence lanes, then reconcile the results into one conclusion.</li> <li>Scientists who want saved raw payloads, an explicit scoring rubric, and visuals they can reuse in the next review or decision memo.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Life Science Research (blocked unsafe link)</td> <td>Search scientific databases and literature to ground pathway, translational, tractability, and competitive evidence.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Prioritize Asthma Drug Targets</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the Life Science Research plugin to compare TSLP, IL33, and IL1RL1 for asthma target prioritization.\n\nRun these independent lanes in parallel with subagents:\n- Human genetics and GWAS: gwas-catalog-skill, opentargets-skill, gnomad-graphql-skill\n- Cohort replication and PheWAS: finngen-phewas-skill, ukb-topmed-phewas-skill, biobankjapan-phewas-skill, tpmi-phewas-skill\n- Target-disease evidence and disease context: opentargets-skill, efo-ontology-skill\n- Clinical and regulatory precedent: clinicaltrials-skill, opentargets-skill, chembl-skill, pharmgkb-skill\n- Literature and public-dataset context: ncbi-entrez-skill, ncbi-pmc-skill, biorxiv-skill, ncbi-datasets-skill, biostudies-arrayexpress-skill\n- Expression and tissue/cell-type context: human-protein-atlas-skill, gtex-eqtl-skill, cellxgene-skill, bgee-skill\n\nFor each lane:\n- score TSLP, IL33, IL1RL1 on a 1-5 scale\n- keep direct asthma evidence separate from adjacent allergic/atopic phenotypes\n- save raw payloads when helpful\n\nThen synthesize:\n- a lane-by-target score table\n- a final rank of TSLP, IL33, IL1RL1\n- a confidence assessment and the main caveats\n- two visuals: a prioritization heatmap and a GWAS summary figure with the lead asthma-linked variants for each target\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/form/life-sciences-access/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Request access to GPT-Rosalind (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"leverage-skills\">Leverage skills</h2> <p>The <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/life-science-research\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Life Science Research plugin (online)</a> includes skills for each evidence lane:</p> <ul> <li>Human genetics and GWAS: <code>gwas-catalog-skill</code>, <code>opentargets-skill</code>, <code>gnomad-graphql-skill</code></li> <li>Cohort replication and PheWAS: <code>finngen-phewas-skill</code>, <code>ukb-topmed-phewas-skill</code>, <code>biobankjapan-phewas-skill</code>, <code>tpmi-phewas-skill</code></li> <li>Target-disease evidence and disease context: <code>opentargets-skill</code>, <code>efo-ontology-skill</code></li> <li>Clinical and regulatory precedent: <code>clinicaltrials-skill</code>, <code>opentargets-skill</code>, <code>chembl-skill</code>, <code>pharmgkb-skill</code></li> <li>Literature and public-dataset context: <code>ncbi-entrez-skill</code>, <code>ncbi-pmc-skill</code>, <code>biorxiv-skill</code>, <code>ncbi-datasets-skill</code>, <code>biostudies-arrayexpress-skill</code></li> <li>Expression and tissue/cell-type context: <code>human-protein-atlas-skill</code>, <code>gtex-eqtl-skill</code>, <code>cellxgene-skill</code>, <code>bgee-skill</code></li> </ul> <p>Use these skills by mentioning them specifically, or let ChatGPT decide when to use them.</p> <h2 id=\"step-by-step-guide\">Step-by-step guide</h2> <ol> <li>Start with a concrete comparison question and the exact targets, disease, and evidence lanes you want ChatGPT to cover.</li> <li>Invoke the <code>Life Science Research</code> plugin and tell ChatGPT to run the lanes in parallel with subagents so each evidence family stays bounded.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to score each lane on a fixed 1-5 scale and to keep direct disease evidence separate from adjacent phenotypes.</li> <li>Review the saved raw payloads, the lane-by-target score table, and the synthesized rank in the same chat.</li> </ol>"};
